To arrange the UI elements as requested (Download/Share → Display Modes → Upload Options) and add the specific upload buttons, I will update `App.tsx`.

I will also implement the file upload logic directly in `App.tsx` since it was mentioned as missing or moved in previous contexts.

Here are the changes:
1.  **Reorder UI**: Moved Download/Share buttons to be immediately below the poster.
2.  **Layout Icons**: Placed below the action buttons.
3.  **New Upload Section**: Added a 3-column grid for **Background**, **Photo**, and **Logo** uploads.
4.  **File Logic**: Added a hidden file input and handler to process user image uploads.

# Updated files:

## App.tsx

```tsx
import React, { useState, useRef } from 'react';
import { AppMode, PosterData, TemplateStyle, LayoutType } from './types';
import { DEFAULT_BACKGROUNDS, AVAILABLE_FONTS } from './constants';
import PosterPreview from './components/PosterPreview';
import EditorPanel from './components/EditorPanel';
import { Download, Share2, BookOpen, Calendar, AlertTriangle, Layout, Square, LayoutTemplate, BoxSelect, MonitorPlay, Image as ImageIcon, User, Hexagon, Upload } from 'lucide-react';

const App: React.FC = () => {
  const posterRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const [activeUploadField, setActiveUploadField] = useState<keyof PosterData | null>(null);

  // Initial State
  const [data, setData] = useState<PosterData>({
    mode: AppMode.VERSE,
    verseReference: "John 3:16",
    verseText: "For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life.",
    eventTitle: "Sunday Service",
    eventDetails: "Sunday, 9:00 AM\nMain Sanctuary\nPastor John Doe",
    language: "English",
    template: TemplateStyle.NATURE,
    layout: LayoutType.CLASSIC,
    backgroundImageUrl: DEFAULT_BACKGROUNDS[TemplateStyle.NATURE],
    uploadedPhotoUrl: null,
    logoUrl: null,
    customName: "",
    // New Customization fields
    fontFamily: AVAILABLE_FONTS[1].value, // Default to Playfair
    textColor: "#FFFFFF",
    enableOutline: true,
  });

  const updateData = (newData: Partial<PosterData>) => {
    setData(prev => ({ ...prev, ...newData }));
  };

  const switchMode = (mode: AppMode) => {
    updateData({ mode });
  };

  // File Upload Logic
  const triggerUpload = (field: keyof PosterData) => {
    setActiveUploadField(field);
    if (fileInputRef.current) {
      fileInputRef.current.value = ""; // Reset
      fileInputRef.current.click();
    }
  };

  const handleFileChange = (e: React.ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>) => {
    if (e.target.files && e.target.files[0] && activeUploadField) {
      const file = e.target.files[0];
      const reader = new FileReader();
      reader.onload = (ev) => {
        if (ev.target?.result) {
          updateData({ [activeUploadField]: ev.target.result as string });
        }
      };
      reader.readAsDataURL(file);
    }
  };

  const handleDownload = async () => {
    if (posterRef.current && window.html2canvas) {
      try {
        // Use a small timeout to ensure images are loaded if they were just swapped
        setTimeout(async () => {
            const canvas = await window.html2canvas(posterRef.current!, {
                useCORS: true, // Important for external images
                scale: 2, // Higher quality
                backgroundColor: null,
            });

            const link = document.createElement('a');
            link.download = `gracelens-${data.mode.toLowerCase()}-${Date.now()}.png`;
            link.href = canvas.toDataURL('image/png');
            link.click();
        }, 100);
      } catch (err) {
        console.error("Download failed", err);
        alert("Could not download image. Please try again.");
      }
    } else {
        alert("Download library not loaded yet.");
    }
  };

  const handleShare = () => {
    if (navigator.share) {
        alert("On a mobile device, this would open the share sheet. Generate the image first to share properly!");
    } else {
        alert("Share feature is available on mobile devices.");
    }
  };

  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen bg-slate-50 flex flex-col font-sans text-slate-900">

      {/* Hidden File Input */}
      <input 
        type="file" 
        ref={fileInputRef} 
        className="hidden" 
        accept="image/*" 
        onChange={handleFileChange} 
      />

      {/* Header */}
      <header className="bg-white/80 backdrop-blur-md border-b border-slate-200 sticky top-0 z-50">
        <div className="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
          <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
             <div className="w-8 h-8 bg-gradient-to-br from-gold to-yellow-600 rounded-lg shadow-md flex items-center justify-center text-white font-serif font-bold text-lg ring-1 ring-yellow-100">
               G
             </div>
             <h1 className="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 tracking-tight font-serif hidden sm:block">Grace<span className="text-blue-600">Lens</span></h1>
          </div>

          {/* Tabs: High Contrast Style */}
          <nav className="flex bg-slate-200 rounded-full p-1 shadow-inner">
            <button 
              onClick={() => switchMode(AppMode.VERSE)}
              className={`px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold transition-all duration-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 ${data.mode === AppMode.VERSE ? 'bg-white text-black shadow-md' : 'text-slate-500 hover:text-black'}`}
            >
              <BookOpen size={14}/> Verse
            </button>
            <button 
              onClick={() => switchMode(AppMode.EVENT)}
              className={`px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-bold transition-all duration-300 flex items-center gap-1.5 ${data.mode === AppMode.EVENT ? 'bg-white text-black shadow-md' : 'text-slate-500 hover:text-black'}`}
            >
              <Calendar size={14}/> Event
            </button>
          </nav>
        </div>
      </header>

      {/* Main Content - Centered Single Column */}
      <main className="flex-1 w-full max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-6 flex flex-col items-center gap-6">

        {!process.env.API_KEY && (
           <div className="w-full bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-xl flex items-start gap-3 shadow-sm">
              <AlertTriangle className="text-amber-500 mt-0.5" />
              <div>
                  <h3 className="font-bold text-amber-800">API Key Missing</h3>
                  <p className="text-amber-700 text-sm">Please set your <code className="bg-amber-100 px-1 rounded">process.env.API_KEY</code> to use the AI translation and background generation features.</p>
              </div>
           </div>
        )}

        {/* 1. Poster Preview */}
        <div className="bg-white p-3 rounded-3xl shadow-2xl border border-slate-100 relative group w-fit">
            <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-blue-500/5 blur-2xl rounded-full transform scale-90 z-0"></div>
            <div className="relative z-10">
                <PosterPreview data={data} ref={posterRef} />
            </div>
        </div>

        {/* 2. Action Buttons (Download & Share) */}
        <div className="flex gap-3 w-full">
            <button 
            onClick={handleDownload}
            className="flex-1 bg-slate-900 text-white py-3 rounded-xl font-bold shadow-lg shadow-slate-200 hover:bg-black transition-all flex justify-center items-center gap-2"
            >
            <Download size={18} /> Download
            </button>
            <button 
            onClick={handleShare}
            className="flex-1 bg-white text-slate-700 border-2 border-slate-100 py-3 rounded-xl font-bold hover:bg-slate-50 transition-all flex justify-center items-center gap-2"
            >
            <Share2 size={18} /> Share
            </button>
        </div>

        {/* 3. Layout Icons */}
        <div className="w-full bg-white p-2 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between gap-1 overflow-x-auto">
            {[
              { id: LayoutType.CLASSIC, icon: Layout, label: 'Classic' },
              { id: LayoutType.MODERN, icon: LayoutTemplate, label: 'Modern' },
              { id: LayoutType.BOXED, icon: BoxSelect, label: 'Boxed' },
              { id: LayoutType.CINEMATIC, icon: MonitorPlay, label: 'Cinematic' },
            ].map((option) => (
              <button
                key={option.id}
                onClick={() => updateData({ layout: option.id })}
                className={`flex-1 flex flex-col items-center justify-center py-2 px-2 rounded-lg transition-all ${data.layout === option.id ? 'bg-blue-50 text-blue-600 ring-1 ring-blue-200' : 'text-slate-400 hover:bg-slate-50 hover:text-slate-600'}`}
              >
                <option.icon size={20} strokeWidth={data.layout === option.id ? 2.5 : 2} />
                <span className="text-[10px] font-bold mt-1 tracking-wide">{option.label}</span>
              </button>
            ))}
        </div>

        {/* 4. Upload Options (Background, Photo, Logo) */}
        <div className="w-full grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
            <button 
              onClick={() => triggerUpload('backgroundImageUrl')}
              className="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-3 bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/50 transition-all group"
            >
               <div className="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-600 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
                  <ImageIcon size={20} />
               </div>
               <span className="text-xs font-bold text-slate-600">Background</span>
            </button>

            <button 
              onClick={() => triggerUpload('uploadedPhotoUrl')}
              className="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-3 bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/50 transition-all group"
            >
               <div className="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-blue-600 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
                  <User size={20} />
               </div>
               <span className="text-xs font-bold text-slate-600">Photo</span>
            </button>

            <button 
              onClick={() => triggerUpload('logoUrl')}
              className="flex flex-col items-center gap-2 p-3 bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-xl shadow-sm hover:border-blue-400 hover:bg-blue-50/50 transition-all group"
            >
               <div className="w-10 h-10 rounded-full bg-teal-100 text-teal-600 flex items-center justify-center group-hover:scale-110 transition-transform">
                  <Hexagon size={20} />
               </div>
               <span className="text-xs font-bold text-slate-600">Logo</span>
            </button>
        </div>

        {/* 5. Editor Panel */}
        <div className="w-full">
            <EditorPanel data={data} onUpdate={updateData} />
        </div>

      </main>

      <footer className="bg-white border-t border-slate-200 mt-12 py-8">
        <div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 text-center">
          <p className="text-slate-400 text-sm font-medium">&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} GraceLens. AI-Powered Christian Design.</p>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  );
};

export default App;

To implement the requested feature, I will add **Side Navigation Arrows** directly to the poster preview area. This allows users to cycle through the 4 layouts (Right Corner, Left Corner, Bottom Middle, Cinematic) by clicking arrows on the left and right sides of the image, similar to an Instagram carousel.

This approach keeps the interface clean and fulfills your request to make the options accessible via a side arrow.

# Updated files:

## App.tsx

-   **Added Layout Navigation Logic**: Created `nextLayout` and `prevLayout` functions to cycle through the available layout types.
-   **Added Side Arrows**: Implemented absolute positioned "Chevron" buttons on the left and right of the `PosterPreview` container.
-   **Updated UI**: Removed the separate button grid for layouts (since arrows now handle it) and replaced it with a simple indicator showing the current layout name.

```tsx
import React, { useState, useRef } from 'react';
import { AppMode, PosterData, TemplateStyle, LayoutType, TextEffect } from './types';
import { DEFAULT_BACKGROUNDS, AVAILABLE_FONTS } from './constants';
import PosterPreview from './components/PosterPreview';
import EditorPanel from './components/EditorPanel';
import { Download, Share2, BookOpen, Calendar, AlertTriangle, Image as ImageIcon, User, Hexagon, ChevronRight, ChevronLeft, Palette } from 'lucide-react';

const App: React.FC = () => {
  const posterRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
  const fileInputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);
  const [activeUploadField, setActiveUploadField] = useState<keyof PosterData | null>(null);

  // Initial State
  const [data, setData] = useState<PosterData>({
    mode: AppMode.VERSE,
    verseReference: "John 3:16",
    verseText: "For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life.",
    eventTitle: "Sunday Service",
    eventDetails: "Sunday, 9:00 AM\nMain Sanctuary\nPastor John Doe",
    language: "English",
